 "text": "This clause is enforceable because it complies with the statutory rules governing rent increases under **section 116** of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*. \n\nSpecifically, section 116(1) requires a landlord to give a tenant at least 90 days' written notice before increasing the rent, and section 116(3) requires that the notice be in a form approved by the Landlord and Tenant Board and set out the landlord's intention to increase the rent along with the amount of the new rent. Because the lease clause aligns with these mandatory statutory requirements rather than attempting to reduce or waive them, it does not conflict with the Act and is valid.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 116",
